      "writtenOn": "2020-02-18T19:43:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t believe this changes the outcome/behavior, since GPIO and GPIO_INT  are simply consumed in the immediately following:\n\n```\n/* GPIO signal list. */\nconst struct gpio_info gpio_list[] \u003d {\n\t#include \"gpio.wrap\"\n};\n```\n\nBefore, GPIO_INT was defined as GPIO(name, pin, flags), so I am simply expanding it here.\n\n---\n\nThe inability to have dependence on other macros is the one compromise area of this mechanism, but it seemed minor compared to having forced gpio.inc order.",
